@namespace Fravashi.Web.Components.Settings

@* Settings > Connections > Credential broker (work item #357; it was a block of the Environment overview). The card
   itself is unchanged: it holds every broker setting there is (enable, endpoint, mint, revoke). *@
<div class="page-body-content" data-testid="broker-settings">
    <h2>Credential broker</h2>
    <p class="studio-muted">
        The corporate / untrusted-client credential tier (ADR 0010). When enabled, @(ProductName.Short) signs you in through
        your identity provider and mints a short-lived, per-user token from a remote broker - the organization's
        shared key stays on the broker and never reaches this device. Revoke here to cut this device off
        immediately. This is off in the single-user default.
    </p>
    <BrokerConnectionCard />
</div>
